          "contents": "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n\n# TODO 1: Fix the definition of practice_shots\npractice_shots = [5, 15, 25, 40, 50]\nmade_shots = [3, 6.5, 9.5, 14, 15]\n\n# This line confirms how many examples the data holds:\nprint(\"Data loaded:\", len(practice_shots), \"examples\")\n\n# This line creates a new, untrained model:\nmodel = LinearRegression()\n\n# This line trains the model on the client's data:\nmodel.fit(practice_shots, made_shots)\n\n# TODO 2: Predict the value you made on paper\n",
